    "evidence": "Re-reviewed 2026-08-08. Ethereum Frankencoin exposes minterOnly burnFrom(owner, amount), which calls the internal burn path without spending holder allowance; BridgedFrankencoin likewise documents admitted modules as able to move or burn arbitrary addresses. Current active minters are protocol contracts whose reviewed public entrypoints constrain the payer, so no immediately callable human/admin seizure was established. Governance can, however, admit a new minter after the protocol delay unless vetoed, leaving a concrete token-level arbitrary-holder burn surface and supporting Possible rather than No. Current positions also contain issuer-freezable XAUT, PAXG, WBTC, cbBTC, and tokenized-equity collateral, providing independent Upstream exposure.",
    "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex unfreezable-cohort audit",
    "reviewedAt": "2026-08-08"
  },
  "oracleRisk": {
    "tier": "oracleless",
    "summary": "Frankencoin positions use challenge auctions to determine collateral market price and liquidate unsuccessful positions, so the liquidation path does not depend on an external price oracle.",
    "role": "coin-price-feed",
    "branchModel": "single-path",
    "branchApplicability": {
      "disposition": "not-applicable",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-07-14",
      "reviewer": "Codex data review",
      "rationale": "Frankencoin documents position liquidation through permissionless challenges and auctions. The auction determines the collateral market price and liquidates a position when the highest bid remains below its liquidation price, so there is no collateral-price oracle branch to enumerate.",
